{"page":493527,"revision":1376891610,"ref":"o1","kind":"subject","cue":"lead","strength":"normal","name":"Order","span":[0,822],"text":"In mathematics, the order of a finite group is the number of its elements. If a group is not finite, one says that its order is infinite.","links":[{"title":"Linear map"},{"title":"Shear mapping"},{"title":"Function composition"},{"title":"Mathematics"},{"title":"Finite group"},{"title":"Group (mathematics)"}],"hash":"sha256:4895e1add305d319737435d9174ca7bd8923c5276c09f7c94b0a3855ca1f2fce","flags":["more-citations-needed","informal"],"extractor":"m2/v0.3.8"}
